        f(x-h_l) = f(x) - h_l f'(x) + {h_l}^2  \frac{f''(x)}{2} - {h_l}^3 \frac{f'''(\xi_2)}{6}, \xi_2 \in (x, x-h_l) \\
    \end{aligned}

Using the fact that :math:`f \in C^3` and solving the linear system, we derive:

.. math::
    f'(x) \approx \frac{ {h_l}^2 f(x+h_r) - {h_r}^2 f(x-h_l)
